@startuml provision-retire-recovery
title M-UM2: provision, retire and crash recovery (v0 design; v1 egress annotations)

participant "Configured caller\ninstaller / dispatcher / swarma-operator UID" as C
participant "sudo\ntrusted root transition" as S
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; one invocation; no arguments" as M
database "Root-owned state\npolicy, ledger/cursor, lock, journal, audit\nv1 applied state" as R
participant "OS account backend / kernel\nmacOS or Linux; root operations" as O
database "Homes (account-owned)\nquarantine / metadata export (root-controlled)" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nservice UID; owns bindings / leases" as B
participant "Approved workspace executors\nchild UID; fixed environment; design labels" as W
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot; separate invocation" as L
database "Admitted complete-content custody\noutside child home and retirement deletion\nlocation/transport unpublished" as T

note over C,L
  [[../spec/helper.md#43-usercreate Defining spec §4.3 create]], [[../spec/helper.md#44-userretire §4.4 retire]],
  [[../spec/helper.md#441-retirement-deletion-and-metadata-export §4.4.1 deletion/export]], [[../spec/helper.md#46-lock-journal-and-idempotency §4.6 recovery]].
  Current: unimplemented; v0 accounts/static range deny, v1 account narrowing, v2 grant verification (§13).
  SH2+ joint admission gate I4 remains closed; dispatcher alone invokes the launcher (§§7, 14).
  Each helper request <= 16 KiB, one JSON document in 5 s (§2).
end note

note over C,S
  R-OPERATOR (§§2-3, 11): operator is protected swarma-operator UID, never a harness account.
  Phone: hardware-backed biometric operator device key; tailnet SSH, forced operator command, no shell.
  Machine verifies pinned-key signature over this act only; app shows exact who/actions/until.
  Terminal: password sudo into operator, no NOPASSWD, timestamp_timeout=0.
  Operator helper sudo authenticated and non-cached; NOPASSWD only dispatcher helper/launcher.
  Widening: authentication + exact-content confirmation; refused inside agent sessions.
  Narrowing: authentication only except R-ALLSTOP needs one confirmation; revocation: one biometric confirmation.
  Human status/grants/accounts/bindings reads via swarma-observer without confirmation.
  Observer has no mutation/launcher or other principal's private effect.observe access.
  Entry/signature/read interfaces and phone-to-helper transition unpublished (§14 question 17).
end note

== Before each invocation: intake, transition lock and dependency recovery (§§2-3, 4.6) ==
C -> S: exact helper path; no args; helper-op/1 on stdin
S -> M: root; decimal trusted SUDO_UID identifies caller
break Invalid intake / role / ownership / quota; grants in v0/v1
  M --> C: refuse; closed operation schema
end
M -> R: acquire exclusive durable lock (shared by both binaries)
M -> R: validate shared integrity, ALL UID reservations and accounting
M -> R: recover only operation prerequisites within finite budget; compare OS objects
alt Interrupted creation
  M -> O: roll back creation steps
  M -> H: roll back creation steps
else Interrupted stop / retirement prerequisite
  M -> M: continue same admitted effect; bounded forward batches
else Safely classified unrelated retirement
  M -> M: keep reservation/fence; requested control can proceed
end
M -> R: for mutations: check (caller principal, request_id) and canonical operation/args
break Mutation: TERMINAL same effect and same arguments
  M --> C: recorded result + target CURRENT state; never repeat terminal action
end
break Mutation: same ID, different arguments
  M --> C: request_id_conflict
end
note over M,R
  R-OUTCOME: pre-admission refusal has no intent; retry needs fresh authority.
  Pending stop/retire continues same ID/canonical args; never terminal refusal replay.
  Transport uncertainty alone never proves pending intent.
  Mutation sequences below describe new effects or pending recovery.
  effect.observe is a separate read-only invocation, outside the mutation replay/create path.
end note

note over M,O
  user.create service: installer configured for these names or operator may create
  protected swarma-operator and swarma-observer; dispatcher cannot (§4.3).
  Neither hosts a harness session or has launcher authority.
  Ordinary service non-login backend does not claim to admit forced SSH;
  operator/observer narrow OS entry settings need publication/qualification (§14 question 17).
end note

== Read-only effect.observe (R-OBS, §§2, 4.5-4.6) ==
C -> S: effect.observe helper-op/1; original effect request_id,\noperation and canonical-argument digest (exact encoding unpublished)
S -> M: root; trusted SUDO_UID identifies observing caller
M -> R: acquire same exclusive lock; dependency recovery first; authenticate original caller or operator;\nserialize observation with receiver journal and recovery
break Observing principal is neither original caller nor operator
  M --> C: refuse observation; no private journal exposure
end
M -> R: read caller/effect mapping, result, target state and rollback/removal evidence
M --> C: recorded (result + current state), pending, rolled_back,\nnot_recorded, unavailable or contradictory
note over C,R
  not_recorded requires complete authoritative coverage; expired/missing/unreadable evidence = unavailable.
  Mutation grant expiry does not prevent authenticated original-principal observation.
  Retain effect/removal evidence until original identities permanently inadmissible;
  concrete bounds and authoritative-coverage rule unpublished (§14 question 8).
  Observation never creates/relaunches; rolled_back/not_recorded do not authorise new create.
  Dispatcher maps recorded by current state; rolled_back/not_recorded -> known absent for effect only;
  Pending is admitted effect handling, never terminal refusal; target/process liveness may be unknown.
  pending/unavailable -> unknown liveness; contradictory -> contradictory (§5).
end note

== Installation before any agent account (§§8, 11) ==
C -> O: installer: helper-owned parent anchor/table + static range deny
note over C,O: R-RANGE-DENY: UIDs 30000-59999; v0 admits platform proxy listeners only.\nLinux skuid range every protocol + counters/logs; macOS pf user range + sandbox beyond TCP/UDP.
C -> O: dedicated test-UID active precedence probe at install / service start / schedule
break Failed or unknown range precedence proof
  C -> R: incident; drop enforced readiness; no activation
end

== user.create (§§4.1-4.3) ==
M -> R: under shared lock refuse persisted all-stop mark;\nreconcile pre-act create intent behind authoritative closed frontier (§8.3)
M -> R: choose round-robin UID/GID; fresh random 128-bit generation (R-GEN), never counter/reused
M -> O: check directory service and ledger availability;
M -> O: before UID reuse check platform and temporary areas for owned files
break Dirty UID / unmanaged name or home / exhausted range
  M --> C: uid_not_clean / user_exists_unmanaged / home_exists_unmanaged / range_exhausted
end
M -> R: journal planned/completed steps before acting; state creating
M -> O: create account + same-name primary group; no supplementary groups;
M -> O: locked password, hidden; exact UID/GID/home; no supplementary groups
note over M,O: Agent/ordinary-service no-login shell; operator/observer qualified narrow-entry exception (§4.3).\nDeny cron/at and qualify per-OS persistence denial.\nWorkplace fixed root relay shell requires joint backend and helper v1; service executor outside UID.
M -> H: descriptor-relative empty home; account owner; mode 0700
opt v1 enforced profile (MANDATORY for workplace)
  M -> O: denial + verified fw.apply applied state before activation / first launch
  note over M,O: Workplace zero egress: no loopback/proxy exception.\nLinux namespace + Unix-only families; macOS deny-network sandbox + per-UID deny.\nR-NETBIND: account_generation / profile_ref / service_generation / served_policy_digest, not owner alone.\nOne profile-bound listener per bound account generation; row admits only its own proxy.port.\nNo direct/external-http-proxy for any platform account class; N15 revision 2026-10-13 (§8).\nService rows use installer/operator; R-SVC-EGRESS schedule/DNS qualification (§8).
  note over M,O: Whole matrix without evidence refuses fw_unsupported (§8); creation failure rolls back.
end
alt Creation fails or crashes at a step boundary
  note over M,R: Crash stops invocation; next dependent invocation recovers within budget (§4.6).
  M -> O: roll back creation, comparing OS objects with journal
  M -> H: roll back creation
  note over M,H: Exact per-step rollback order / firewall rollback details: unspecified in spec §§4.3, 4.6, 8.
else Creation succeeds
  M -> R: verify recorded admission class, host matrix, exec profile and socket set;\nuntrusted needs v1/ceilings/no shared services/no local loop/no binding or lease
  M -> R: recheck all-stop mark and closed-create frontier before activation;\npersist active only if clear; record result and audit line
  M --> C: username, UID/GID, home, generation, state active
end

== R-TRANSFER: dispatcher workspace contract (§7) ==
opt Dispatcher workspace round (separate invocations before ordinary retirement)
C -> L: dispatcher launches approved swarma-workspace-materialize before work
L -> W: child UID; fixed environment; immutable admitted plan
W -> W: verify archive paths, Git kind/mode and content against immutable-B manifest
break Mismatch, missing or extra archive entry
  W --> C: refuse materialization; no worker start
end
W -> H: verified B standalone repository; fresh config, no hooks/remotes/helpers
note over C,H: Prepare resolves machine-owned exec selection; input/1 pins identity + immutable body digest.\nLauncher verifies same pin at start/retry, refuses drift or all-stop mark.\nPlan digest covers B, mode-aware manifest digest, write scope, exec profile, task-resource digests,\napproved exporter digest, cap values and per-round bounded repair budget.\nCaller supplies bounded canonical tree archive; dispatcher relays/journals digest, holds no repository.
note over C,H: Platform materializes task resources read-only next to workspace; data, never instructions.\nTrusted side gathers/checks/attaches board resources; signed-letter attachments for remote.\nMore requested by letter/outcome; worker never fetches. Formats/caps/placement unpublished (§8).\nWeb default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only; no default search/fetch or donor web server.\nOperator trusted-circle admission only enables donor-side opt-ins; host boundaries stay.\nLocal web-tool service owns account/row/listener; local opted-in agents use Unix socket + grant only.\nWorkplaces never reach it; donor web service separate from harness/bridge (§8).
C -> M: dispatcher account-wide exec.stop after round outcome; workplace tool-write + SSH-ingress fences
M -> O: stop and confirm no account process remains (§4.7)
break Absence failed / partial / unknown
  M --> C: no export admission; retain cleanup obligation
end
note over C,L
  [[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 cleanup admission and disposition]].
  Original-admission consent bounds cleanup after ordinary caller/allocation expiry:
  exact generation/round/exporter/base/manifest/scope, active generation only.
  No harness/lease/network/new task/ordinary successor/worker repair; no R-SESSION reuse.
  Revocation/compromise/ALLSTOP/maintenance/restore holds never bypassed;
  invalid cleanup authority -> explicit operator recovery/export or per-act waiver decision.
  Bounded cleanup capacity/progress; actual resource/storage accounting and fences remain.
  Materialize/work/export each has distinct claim, E-launch/E-stop, root receipt and absence;
  result execution_id names work, not exporter. Ambiguous starts reconcile original evidence.
end note
C -> L: approved swarma-workspace-export ONLY after confirmed absence\nnew linked physical execution/effects, valid work or bounded cleanup admission
L -> W: child UID; fixed environment; no network
W -> H: no-follow kind/mode + content comparison with immutable manifest; skip .git\nmode-only/type-only modify; deletion prior mode; stop at first cap excess
W --> C: complete export outcome; no partial success
alt Deterministic policy refusal / classified source-entry permission failure
  C -> C: retain obligation + immutable refusal effect/result; no C
  alt Current work authority + separate continuation + remaining admitted repair budget
    C -> H: reopen tool-write/SSH ingress ONLY for new linked same-workspace repair turn
    C -> L: separately admit repair execution; preserve valid edits, no re-materialization
    note over C,W: Caller/worker receive class + known offending path only, never partial changes.\nRefused receipt unchanged; new turn/effects, then re-fence + confirm UID absence\nand admit a new complete export by this same contract (§7).
  else No admitted repair
    C -> C: retain home/account/UID/live-allocation quota; execution capacity released on absence\nper-act operator waiver is the only discard path; standing discard off
  end
else Interrupted / unknown / infrastructure or storage failure
  C -> C: pending/unresolved SAME effect/canonical args; reconcile original evidence
else Complete result and blobs available
  C -> T: digest/size verify result + EVERY referenced blob; establish admitted durable custody
  alt Complete-content receipt available
    C -> C: journal complete-content receipt; discharge export obligation
    C --> C: separately authenticate original requester under CURRENT release authority
    note over C,T: Retain until authenticated import acknowledgement or explicit authorized release;\nbounded storage accounting, no silent pre-import expiry or stale-signature release.\nHome retirement need not await import once complete content survives independently.
  else Missing/corrupt blob, storage failure or incomplete durability evidence
    C -> C: keep obligation pending; no deletion or truncation
  end
end
note over C,W: Terminal effects replay retained result, never rerun or replace receipt.\nNew linked re-observation compares recorded/refused class and recorded change-set digest\non same quiesced tree; conflicts contradictory, walk-order diagnostics not compared.\nSource-entry denial classification/typed failure unpublished; no schema extension.\nInfrastructure denial remains unresolved; never chmod or elevate exporter privilege.\nAuthorized discard is a separate journaled per-act operator waiver (§4.4).
note over W,H: Special files/.git variants/collisions/gitlinks/root escape/cap excess refuse WHOLE export.\nDispatcher Revision 0.11 §5.2.1 owns DRAFT result fields; unchanged field set.\nArchive/transport/retention/caps/cleanup interlocks and qualification remain gated (§14 question 15).
end

== user.retire (§4.4): forward recovery only ==
note over C,M
  Dispatcher confirms any broker unbind before retirement (§10); untrusted class never binds/leases.
  Direct operator retirement needs no broker; unconfirmed binding cleanup stays durable
  at dispatcher/operator boundary, never a helper unbind receipt.
  R-TIME: expiry destruction also needs boot-inclusive monotonic lifetime; explicit retirement works.
  Create/bind/launch/stop/unbind/retire have distinct effect IDs;
  retry each effect with its same ID (§5).
  Retirement deletes the home; no archive/delete/keep selector (§4.4.1).
  Separate explicit swarma-operator home retention: authentication + exact-content confirmation;
  refused inside agent sessions; confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished (§14 questions 1, 17).
end note
alt Ordinary dispatcher retirement
  C -> M: present journaled complete-content receipt under unpublished cleanup interlock
  M -> R: record verified discharge of allocation export obligation
else Direct operator retirement
  C -> M: direct operator retirement explicitly waives export\nauthentication + exact-content confirmation for this act
  M -> R: journal explicit operator waiver
end
break Complete-content discharge absent and no explicit per-act waiver
  M --> C: home deletion held; no silent loss of obligation
end
M -> R: journal steps; persist retiring FIRST (commit point)
note over L,B: Launcher refuses new starts; broker refuses leases for retiring generation.
M -> O: stop per-user service domain where available;
M -> O: TERM every generation UID process; grace; KILL remaining; verify ZERO over quiet period
note over M,O: Same termination set as exec.stop; no session or receipt-time window.
break Processes remain or quiescence not established
  M --> C: processes_remain for remaining processes; stay retiring; retry later
  note over M,O: Unknown/failed observation cannot establish absence (§4.7);\nexact retirement observation error / quiet-period duration: unspecified in spec §4.4.
end
note over M,O: v1 denial remains in place throughout home and account cleanup.
M -> H: same-filesystem move into quarantine
M -> R: journal declared-key destruction under shared lock
M -> H: destroy declared keys through trusted descriptors BEFORE walk
break Key destruction failed or unknown
  M -> R: audit outcome without secrets; remain retiring
  M --> C: retirement pending; no walk
end
note over M,H: Recovery confirms destruction or prior absence before continuing.\nDeclared paths / format unpublished (§14 question 6); never follow links.
loop Finite cleanup quantum; serialized batches, not full walk under one lock
  M -> R: revalidate generation, journal, trusted descriptors, quiescence and keys
  M -> H: bounded no-follow deletion batch; unlink links, never follow
  M -> R: persist batch evidence; retain retiring/UID/quota reservation
  M -> R: release shared lock; unrelated controls and cleanup receive fair progress
  M -> R: reacquire for next admitted quantum; compare protected state again
end
note over M,H: Remaining batches are R-OUTCOME pending under original retire effect.\nNumeric budgets/fairness/resume proof unpublished (§14 question 10).\nOnly verified FULL home cleanup permits next step; daily timer stays metadata-only.
break Required deletion incomplete, failed, partial or unknown (including remaining batches)
  M -> R: audit outcome without secrets; remain retiring
  M --> C: retirement pending; unreadability is not absence
end
opt Closed metadata schema and provenance published and qualified (§14 question 6)
  M -> R: generate metadata only from trusted service records; validate closed schema
  M -> H: publish root 0600 metadata export in root 0700 archive directory
  note over M,H: No agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies; no copying/scanning home.\nUnknown provenance/schema failure prevents export publication (§4.4.1).
end
M -> R: audit quiescence, key destruction, deletion and export outcomes; no secrets
M -> O: bounded batches remove owned files from system/per-user temporary areas; yield lock
break Temporary cleanup incomplete / failed / unknown
  M --> C: retirement pending; retain UID/quota and evidence
end
M -> O: remove account and group
opt v1
  M -> O: remove per-account firewall rules LAST; static range deny remains
end
M -> R: persist removed (generation retained forever); result + audit
note over M,H
  archive.sweep: metadata exports ONLY; age, then oldest until total bound.
  At every retirement and from a daily root timer; preserve live effect/tombstone evidence.
  Installer/operator authority (§§3, 4.4.1).
  Export schema/naming/bounds and audit encoding unpublished (§14 question 6).
  Timer process details beyond root / sweep retry unspecified in spec §4.4.1.
end note
M --> C: username, generation, state removed
note over M,R: Crash after retiring commit: next invocation compares OS objects to journal\nand resumes bounded forward batches by dependency; no rollback to active (§§4.2, 4.6).
note over C,B
  Account retirement is separate from identity revocation (§4.4).
  Dispatcher may revoke only recorded one-shot identities after retirement;
  standing identities remain; only operator may revoke with signed record.
end note
note over M,R
  R-GEN restore: external mark closes broker, launcher, dispatcher and host BEFORE bytes visible.
  Reader epoch floors reject ledger rollback; reconcile surviving inventory/tombstones/receipts.
  Never restore retiring/removed to active; pre-restore coverage unavailable, never not_recorded.
  Epoch/restore formats unpublished; whole-machine rollback not locally detectable (§4.6.1).
end note
@enduml
